MVP EXIT CHECKLIST
==================

[ ] RSS and URL collection works for the approved source set.
[ ] Collection scope, country/language catalog and event categories match
    docs/MVP_REQUIREMENTS.md.
[ ] Raw collected material and provenance are retained.
[ ] Initial multilingual source workflow is supported.
[ ] Source duplicates and known syndication are linked.
[ ] Claims and attribution are extracted or entered and linked to sources.
[ ] Analysts can inspect and correct candidate claims.
[ ] Basic source graph and evidence independence groups are available.
[x] Evidence, contradictions and unresolved gaps are represented.
[ ] Event timeline is available with distinct event/publication/collection times.
[ ] National information matrix supports the selected 10–15 countries.
[ ] Markdown and HTML reports are generated from versioned records.
[ ] High-impact reports require and record human review.
[ ] Tests, security safeguards, documented setup and CI pass.
[ ] No repetition is reported as independent confirmation.
[ ] Occurrence, method and attribution remain separate confidence dimensions.


EXPLICITLY DEFERRED BEYOND MVP
==============================

- Full EU and European NATO coverage and broader strategic-neighborhood
  expansion.
- Automated narrative clustering and advanced contradiction detection.
- Advanced graph analytics, semantic search and analyst dashboard.
- Near-real-time monitoring and specialized satellite/AIS integrations.
- Model ensembles, calibrated uncertainty, anomaly detection and early warning.
- GEWS/Sentinel integrations and advanced collaborative analyst workflows.

These capabilities belong to later phases in ARCHITECTURE.md and must not be
treated as MVP-complete by default.
